[Music]  hey guys and welcome back to monster  maze in my previous video together with  Nintendo black crisis we presented a  general idea of how a traditional  dungeon could work in the sequel to  breath the wild giving sort of an  overview of all the different aspects  that make a dungeon fun to play through  as well as some of the problems that  need to be overcome to make the new  mechanics introduced in breath the wild  work together with the more traditional  game design from the older games if you  haven't watched it yet I highly  recommend that you do check that one out  first before moving on as this one will  go a little bit deeper in some of the  points I covered in that video now this  video is going to be a little bit more  freeform and less scripted as I want to  try to explain my thought process a bit  quicker so without further ado let's get  into it in the previous video you may  have noticed a few snippets of this  quote-unquote hypothetical dungeon now  please keep in mind this is not meant to  be a fully realized level by any means  I basically slap this thing together in  a little over two days as you can  clearly see from this amazing texture  work also architectural II speaking this  place makes very little sense like where  would these broken pillars even have  been attached to or what is the purpose  of all these moving platforms it's a  video game level not much else but aside  from the amateur istic look I did  actually think about how you would be  moving through this structure and the  various ways that you can restrict a  player from progressing too easily but  without taking climbing and paragliding  away entirely one thing to mention up  front and don't quote me on this because  I might be completely wrong but I'm  going to guess that the champion  abilities like Rivoli's Gale are no  longer thing in the sequel all these  abilities were tied to the champion  spirits I mean you can even see the  manifest when you use them and at the  end of the game we can clearly see that  they move on to the afterlife and  honestly I think removing these  abilities from the game would be for the  better as memphis grace alone was pretty  opie in my opinion it's like a fairy but  on steroids the first thing to note  about this dungeon idea is that this  outer wall around the dungeon should  either not  or be made on climb aboard there is  unfortunately the sacrifice we do have  to make to make this example work since  if it was climb aboard Varitek and  slippery or whatever I don't actually  see anything wrong with restricting  climbing on certain surfaces  it's just that in breath the wild it was  a little bit inconsistent like why can I  climb these ice crystals which shouldn't  provide any grip at all but I cannot  climb these very rough looking walls  inside of the divine beast for the sake  of demonstration I'm actually gonna hide  this outer wall for now as it will make  my life a lot easier moving the camera  around as you can see this dungeon is  built around that idea of vertical  traversal I talked so much about in the  previous video where a large part of the  complexity is derived from how you are  going to progress upwards I like this  concept for two reasons one is that it  forces you to be observant about your  surroundings and study the space around  you and two because similar to a dungeon  likes a city in the sky  it just feels awesome to scale these  enormous Heights in real life I don't  really have a fear of heights but I'm  not exactly comfortable with them either  as evident from this clip right here  where I had to shoot footage for a  construction company from atop a 70  meter high crane let's just say that my  legs were shaking a fair bit this tower  design is very reminiscent of the snow a  temple or the water temple with a  central pillar that just goes up and up  accompanied by all these sideway paths  leading into other rooms  obviously the ideas that you start from  the bottom and work your way up  gradually so this right here would be  the entrance first let's go over the  different ways of restricting the player  from simply climbing up and reaching the  top prematurely the first and most  simple one being the use of an overhang  in breath the wild if parts of the wall  stick out too far horizontally you won't  be able to progress up link might be  spider-man but even he has his limits  the second one is on climb above  surfaces as mentioned before this could  be a wall that is either too slippery  because of water or ice or in the case  of this example I used iron bars if  you've ever visited Hyrule castles lock  up you might have noticed you won't be  able to climb those the third option  would be a surface that  actually deals damage and knocks you off  if you get into contact with it  which in the case of this example I used  spikes and I think in the previous video  I also gave an example of a tile that  electrocute you for instance it would  kind of depend on the theme of the  dungeon of course all these methods  combined can prevent link from  progressing up way too easily every  floor has been barred off so you can  only access the parts that you are  supposed to so for instance when you  reach this part right here you won't be  able to use your paraglider to reach  this section hence the spikes or cheat  your way around this platforming section  because of the overhang the idea is that  you hop your way from platform to  platform cling on to this one and then  jump to the next one as soon as they  align and boom you're there then you  hold on to the other side of this  rotating wall to reach the platform on  the other side and then you climb your  way up this wall while avoiding these  moving spikes to reach this platform  right here and from here you can  parrot-like down to the next level  progressing up is again restricted by  this overhang and these bars and from  this level you cannot access any other  place you haven't already been to the  only way up is through to the roof of  this structure right here but how well  this is what I meant by forcing the  player to be observant about their  surroundings when you were still on the  bottom floor near the entrance you might  have been able to see that this ledge  right here has a gap in it and by  putting two and two together you will  understand that you can climb around  this wall and up to the roof I put like  a rope here similar to Skyward Sword and  Twilight Princess but honestly this  could have been anything another bridge  or a small stair this was either me  being lazy or wanting to mix it up and  who knows maybe tightrope walking will  become a thing again from this point the  path splits you can either try to enter  this room right here or climb the ladder  to the next floor to any of these three  rooms some are barred some are locked  and honestly this is where I stopped  carrying how he would exactly progress  further I put some random chests here  and there but this project was already  getting out of hand so they are mostly  there for show obviously any of these  rooms could hold a combat challenge or a  puzzle like the ones we encountered in  the shrines oh and this part right here  with the pillars that's where  one of the gameplay options I talked  about previously could be used namely  jumping from wall to wall I actually  tested this out in breath the wild and  if the walls are close enough together  it actually is doable there are some  problems with the camera which  automatically tries to Center behind  link when he clinks the next wall and  the controls are a bit funky since it  doesn't matter from which perspective  you are looking at the situation you  always have to press down and jump to  perform this move which is a bit  counterintuitive however they could  simply fix this with a new input perhaps  pressing the jump button twice in rapid  succession to perform a wall jump just  spitballing here from this point I  really have nowhere else to go in terms  of progression so let's talk about  something I haven't touched upon as of  yet dungeon items as you might have  noticed from my previous video I love me  some hook shot just the idea that you  can paraglide around and target a wall  pull yourself towards it is just amazing  to me I do realize that if the hook shot  is implemented this whole vertical  design pretty much goes out the window  as from that point on there's little  ways to go but linear maze like  room-to-room dungeon design as anything  with a vertical design like this would  be completely destroyed by the ability  to target any wall or object so if  anything this should either be one of  the last items to be introduced in the  game or the surfaces that you are  allowed to target are little bit more  limited in my first video I used Just  Cause as an example but I imagine that  there are so many more cool items that  could be introduced in breadth a while  too so in that case let's have a little  brainstorming session together sound off  in the comments below if you have a cool  idea regarding an item old or new that  could make it into breath the wild - and  who knows I might even compile them and  include them in a future video with that  said I think I have reached a point  where you all get the idea the sequel to  breath the wild has a lot of potential  and a lot of options when it comes to  integrating the traditional dungeon  design I'm pretty sure that speedrunners  will have a field day with the dungeon  idea like the one I just presented and  completely break it on every conceivable  level as they have done so many times in  the past games in the next episode we  are going to switch gears a bit and look  something else the loam a labyrinths  found in breath the wild and see if  these structures could potentially make  a return in the next game as well as  analyzing their architecture I hope you  look forward to it  I was actually planning to do a 100  